            <ArticleTitle>[Cryodestruction of the anterior lobe of adenohypophysis in terminal patients with prostatic cancer].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>21-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors used a new method of treatment of prostatic cancer--selective stereotactic puncture cryodestruction of the anteriod hypophysis lobe--which prevents water-electrolyte imbalance, relieves pain syndrome due to bone metastases, reduces androgenic stimulation of the prostate, improves quality of life for patients of clinical group IV. The operation is low-traumatic and is not accompanied with serious complications.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
